Well, when I learned sig figs I learned that "12,000." would be 100% 
sure to be counted as 5 sig figs, but that "12,000" was an ambigous 
case that we should avoid ourselves and if encountered should be 
treated as 2 sig figs unless we had good reason to think otherwise. The 
logic being that underestimating sig figs will never cause you to 
misrepresent the nature of the answer, but overestimating sig figs 
could cause your reported value to have digits that are meaningless, 
with no way for the person to tell from the answer.

